meta: issue-7

This allows to map any vim filetype to a [Carbon language](https://github.com/carbon-app/carbon/blob/2cbdcd0cc23d2d2f23736dd3cfbe94134b141191/lib/constants.js#L624-L1048).

Example:

```lua
require('carbon-now').setup({
  language_map = {
    typescriptreact = "typescript"
  },
})
```

Or with a function:

```lua
require('carbon-now').setup({
  language_map = function(filetype)
    if (filetype == "typescriptreact") then
      return "typescript"
    end
  end
})
```

A map of known filetypes has also been added, only containing `typescriptreact` and `javascriptreact` for now.
